    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Настя Фомина — четырнадцать тысяч!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да не важно. Поехали домой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It doesn't matter. Let's go home.' The meaning hinges on 'yes' working together with 'home' in spoken Russian. Vika answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Поехали.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let's go.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'let's go' before landing on 'let's go'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Внимание, результаты!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Attention, the results!' Vika anchors the line on 'attention', while 'results' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Ева — пять тысяч двести.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Eva — five thousand two hundred.' The grammar packs 'Eva' and 'two hundred' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Олег — три тысячи семьсот.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Oleg — three thousand seven hundred.' The meaning hinges on 'Oleg' working together with 'seven hundred' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Илья — девять тысяч.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Ilya — nine thousand.' In Russian, the idea of 'Ilya' flows naturally into 'thousand' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Ну?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well?' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'come on' and finishing on 'come on'. Max answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Молодец. Молодец.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well done. Well done.' Notice how Russian expresses 'well done' and 'well done' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Макс — восемь тысяч девятьсот пятьдесят.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Max — eight thousand nine hundred fifty.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Max' before landing on 'fifty'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "ilya",
      "t": "Выходите. Тихо!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Step out. Quiet!' Notice how Russian expresses 'step out' and 'quiet' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Vika answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Но это не предел.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But that is not the limit.' Vika anchors the line on 'but', while 'limit' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "vika",
      "t": "Настя Фомина — четырнадцать тысяч!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Nastya Fomina — fourteen thousand!' The grammar packs 'Nastya' and 'thousand' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
